{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness","id":1525706,"title":"How would the denizen of Chronicle of Darkness react to World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-20T21:42:37-08:00","id":1525706,"title":"How would the denizen of Chronicle of Darkness react to World of Darkness?","content":"I think it's a intersting story for a fanfiction, but I don't have a lot of time spend reading or playing WoD games, so I don't know how different the World are, and how the characters would react to those difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T22:12:56-08:00","id":1525707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness#post1525706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a intersting story for a fanfiction, but I don't have a lot of time spend reading or playing WoD games, so I don't know how different the World are, and how the characters would react to those difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the population of either is massively made of normal human people utterly oblivious to the realities of the supernatural, so my guess is - wouldn't notice much of a difference, if any? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, WoD might be <b><i>much </i></b>worse off enviromentally, considering the whole &quot;multinational conglomerate that serves as business/armed front for a cthonic conspiracy cult&quot; major antagonist narrative of WtA. CotD has no group near the same level of present existencial threat, except for the God-Machine perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-21-2023, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T22:54:07-08:00","id":1525708,"title":"","content":"Well, something I do know about CofD is that &quot;Mortal&quot; are exposed to the supernatural and live, so they aren't really oblivious to the supernatural, so I think they would notice a difference when they see a supernatural creature that look like the thing from their memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T01:06:45-08:00","id":1525711,"title":"","content":"Culturally, I think the big thing that would shock multiverse travelers would be how stringent the WoD supernaturals tend to be about enforcing secrecy, compared to the more lax CofD approach (as mentioned about, CofD humans are far more prone to do it themselves). As well as many critters in the CofD having a pretty easy time of using violence to clean up loose ends comparatively.<br /> <br /> There are of course, completely different creatures (even ones that share the same name) to deal with as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T02:05:00-08:00","id":1525712,"title":"","content":"I think CofD Mortal would think that WoD are kind of oblivious for not noticing even a little of bit of the supernatural or weirdness around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T03:24:27-08:00","id":1525713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525711#post1525711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Culturally, I think the big thing that would shock multiverse travelers would be how stringent the WoD supernaturals tend to be about enforcing secrecy, compared to the more lax CofD approach (as mentioned about, CofD humans are far more prone to do it themselves).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree here, both vampires and werewolves are sworn to secrecy in CofD, and werewolves suffer a mechanical effect if they allow mortals to know. <br /> <br /> I think the biggest difference a supernatural traveler would notice is how mortal allies are treated, the blood bond is different in Requiem than in Masquerade, I can't help but think VtM's blood bond's slavish obedience would be a shock to a vampire traveler. Likewise I think one of the Uratha would be appalled at how kinfolk are treated. <br /> <br /> I think wraith would be the biggest culture shock though, should anyone used to the dead traveled to WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T03:40:10-08:00","id":1525715,"title":"","content":"There is a fun thread over at RPG.net that you might enjoy:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/n-owod-in-character-crossover-discussions.392895/\" target=\"_blank\">nWOD/oWOD In-character Crossover Discussions</a><br /> <br /> I would note that random human witnesses wouldn't tell the difference between Uratha and Garou, or Unchained and the Fallen. It's just this terrifying thing they though only existed in movies. It would take someone experienced with a supernatural type to see that something is different. Even Hunters may miss out on the subtleties. If a CofD Hunter puts Uratha, Gangrel Vampires, shapechanging Mages and miscellaneous weirdness into the same bag, Garou might not stand out in any particular way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T03:41:35-08:00","id":1525716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525713#post1525713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think wraith would be the biggest culture shock though, should anyone used to the dead traveled to WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are Wraith different from Ghost in CofD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T04:57:52-08:00","id":1525720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525716#post1525716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are Wraith different from Ghost in CofD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraiths aren't substantial different in most ways, but everything else is. Wraiths struggle to visit the living world, there's vast organizations and machinery, even to the point of forging souls into currency (IIRC, it's been a while). Meanwhile in CofD the ghosts typically start in twilight which is basically the skin lands, the individual realms in the underworld are more independent and ruled by godlike beings. <br /> <br /> Now as to ghosts and wraiths specifically, wraiths have a part of themselves urging them towards oblivion but that isn't something that would be immediately obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T05:42:44-08:00","id":1525722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525715#post1525715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a fun thread over at RPG.net that you might enjoy:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/n-owod-in-character-crossover-discussions.392895/\" target=\"_blank\">nWOD/oWOD In-character Crossover Discussions</a><br /> <br /> I would note that random human witnesses wouldn't tell the difference between Uratha and Garou, or Unchained and the Fallen. It's just this terrifying thing they though only existed in movies. It would take someone experienced with a supernatural type to see that something is different. Even Hunters may miss out on the subtleties. If a CofD Hunter puts Uratha, Gangrel Vampires, shapechanging Mages and miscellaneous weirdness into the same bag, Garou might not stand out in any particular way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very much this - i get the feeling some people have an exagerated idea of the average person degree of awareness &amp; knowledge of the supernatural in CotD-verse.<br /> <br /> It's more of a &quot;people stick to their own little (sometimes private, sometimes communal) key beliefs/superstitions as fact, because they <b>are </b>fact, to them at least&quot; than actual familiarity overall. A few hundred minions, hanger-ons &amp; &quot;people in the know&quot; around each of the big supernatural &quot;courts&quot; will still be a <i>very </i>select clique in a mid to large city in the hundreds of thousands of inhabitants, what to say of metropolises counting their numbers in the millions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T06:13:34-08:00","id":1525725,"title":"","content":"A random person from CofD (2023) get sent to cWoD (1991), how would they react? And how much would the supernatural affect them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 11-21-2023, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T06:20:09-08:00","id":1525726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525716#post1525716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are Wraith different from Ghost in CofD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraiths are souls of the dead, while Ghosts are explicitly not - they're sapient echoes of the dead. It's a very esoteric difference that wouldn't be obvious to mundane witnesses, or even to the dead themselves - both Wraiths and Ghosts are people, after all. Still, the same supernatural powers (Arcanoi or Ceremonies) and cosmic forces (Oblivion or the Underworld) may affect Wraiths and Ghosts differently as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T06:30:41-08:00","id":1525727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525725#post1525725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A random person from CofD (2023) get sent to cWoD (1991), how would they react? And how much would the supernatural affect them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spend some hours confused then trying to avoid any chance of accidentally seducing his own mother and come up with a way to go Back to the Future<sup>tm</sup>\u200b? Who knows, i'm in the dark either way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T06:32:47-08:00","id":1525728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525727#post1525727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who knows, i'm in the dark either way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You never played Classic World of Darkness?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T06:48:35-08:00","id":1525729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525728#post1525728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You never played Classic World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, whichever world one chronicles, darkness pervades all the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Just being facetious - damn, i remember a time when half the Cam-related clanbooks were still unpublished....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T08:36:18-08:00","id":1525732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525713#post1525713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to disagree here, both vampires and werewolves are sworn to secrecy in CofD, and werewolves suffer a mechanical effect if they allow mortals to know.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest difference a supernatural traveler would notice is how mortal allies are treated, the blood bond is different in Requiem than in Masquerade, I can't help but think VtM's blood bond's slavish obedience would be a shock to a vampire traveler. Likewise I think one of the Uratha would be appalled at how kinfolk are treated.<br /> <br /> I think wraith would be the biggest culture shock though, should anyone used to the dead traveled to WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>The blood bond is shit in requiem. Like horrid to be under. Is the blood bond of Masquerade that much worse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T10:22:03-08:00","id":1525735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525732#post1525732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The blood bond is shit in requiem. Like horrid to be under. Is the blood bond of Masquerade that much worse?</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem's is an infatuation, where as Masquerade's is an &quot;all consuming passion.&quot; In requiem the regent gets a bonus to social maneuvers and discipline dice pools, in Masquerade they gain the ability to dominate without eye contact and dominate is harder to resist, but also some thralls will &quot;commit any act, including suicide or murder, for their beloved\u200b&quot;. Lastly resisting the bond is harder in Masquerade, requiring massive amounts of willpower rolls and points spent to act against your regent, while in requiem it's only a breaking point to harm your regent. <br /> <br /> Interesting to me, as I looked into this, was that the wearing away of the bond is kind of balanced between the two systems. In Requiem you have to avoid drinking from your regent for a year, while in Masquerade you have to avoid drinking from, or seeing, your regent, for several months, but less than a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T10:39:33-08:00","id":1525736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525706-how-would-the-denizen-of-chronicle-of-darkness-react-to-world-of-darkness?p=1525735#post1525735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Requiem's is an infatuation, where as Masquerade's is an &quot;all consuming passion.&quot; In 